  "content": {
    "id": "p18-q12-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "12",
    "prompt": "Rearrange each of these formulas to make the pronumeral in brackets the subject. Assume all pronumerals take non-negative values.",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 2,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p18-q12-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$M=\\sqrt{\\frac{ab}{t}+a^2}\\qquad(t)$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$t=\\frac{ab}{M^2-a^2}$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}M^2&=\\frac{ab}{t}+a^2\\\\M^2-a^2&=\\frac{ab}{t}\\\\t(M^2-a^2)&=ab\\\\t&=\\frac{ab}{M^2-a^2}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 42
      },
      {
        "id": "p18-q12-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$V=\\frac13a^2\\sqrt{\\ell^2-\\frac{a^2}{2}}\\qquad(\\ell)$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\ell=\\sqrt{\\frac{9V^2}{a^4}+\\frac{a^2}{2}}$\n\nIsolate the square root, square both sides, then take the non-negative square root.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{3V}{a^2}&=\\sqrt{\\ell^2-\\frac{a^2}{2}}\\\\\\frac{9V^2}{a^4}&=\\ell^2-\\frac{a^2}{2}\\\\\\ell^2&=\\frac{9V^2}{a^4}+\\frac{a^2}{2}\\\\\\ell&=\\sqrt{\\frac{9V^2}{a^4}+\\frac{a^2}{2}}\\end{align*}$$Use the non-negative root because $\\ell\\geq0$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 47
      },
      {
        "id": "p18-q12-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$E=\\frac{w^2a}{(w^2+m)b^3}\\qquad(a)$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$a=\\frac{Eb^3(w^2+m)}{w^2}$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}E(w^2+m)b^3&=w^2a\\\\a&=\\frac{Eb^3(w^2+m)}{w^2}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 28
      },
      {
        "id": "p18-q12-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "$T=2\\pi\\sqrt{\\frac{\\ell+r}{g}}\\qquad(r)$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$r=g\\left(\\frac{T}{2\\pi}\\right)^2-\\ell$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{T}{2\\pi}&=\\sqrt{\\frac{\\ell+r}{g}}\\\\\\left(\\frac{T}{2\\pi}\\right)^2&=\\frac{\\ell+r}{g}\\\\\\ell+r&=g\\left(\\frac{T}{2\\pi}\\right)^2\\\\r&=g\\left(\\frac{T}{2\\pi}\\right)^2-\\ell\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 43
      },
      {
        "id": "p18-q12-e",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "e",
        "prompt": "$x=a\\sqrt{\\frac{k}{ph+y}}\\qquad(h)$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$h=\\frac{ka^2-yx^2}{px^2}$\n\nSquare both sides, clear the denominator, then isolate $h$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}x^2&=\\frac{a^2k}{ph+y}\\\\x^2(ph+y)&=a^2k\\\\px^2h+yx^2&=a^2k\\\\px^2h&=a^2k-yx^2\\\\h&=\\frac{ka^2-yx^2}{px^2}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 52
      },
      {
        "id": "p18-q12-f",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "f",
        "prompt": "$v^2=u^2+2as\\qquad(u)$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$u=\\sqrt{v^2-2as}$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}u^2&=v^2-2as\\\\u&=\\sqrt{v^2-2as}\\end{align*}$$Use the non-negative root because $u\\geq0$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 24
      }
    ]
  },
